(a) whether Government has taken any measures to promote the registration of employees and employers under the Employees' State Insurance Corporation (ESIC);
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) the steps taken by Government to improve access to health services for the beneficiaries of Employees' State Insurance (ESI) scheme;
(d) whether Government has taken any initiative to upgrade or expand ESI facilities across the country;
(e) if so, the details thereof; and
(f) the measures taken to strenghten social security and healthcare benefits for workers through ESIC?

(a) the current status of the Coal Trading Exchange (CTE);
(b) out of the 131 coal blocks allocated under the Commercial Coal Mining Policy the numbers that have commenced actual production as of February, 2026;
(c) the penalties that have been imposed for delays in achieving the milestones;
(d) whether Government has completed the revised Jharia Master Plan for rehabilitation and the new technologies which are being deployed to manage long-standing underground mine fires; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the expected timeline for completing permanent rectification of the remaining black spots out of 13,795 that have been identified on National Highways;
(b) whether Government has any mechanism for public participation in identifying black spots;
(c) the steps being taken to ensure better coordination between the Centre and States to reduce accidents on National Highways;
(d) whether Government is considering the use of AI-based monitoring or sensor-based technology to identify black spots and enhance real-time road safety measures, if so, details thereof; and
(e) the total complaints/ suggestions regarding dangerous roads stretches that have been addressed?

(a) the measures being taken to expedite the processing of PACS applications for petrol/diesel outlets and LPG distributorships;
(b) whether there are any provisions to relax the criteria for PACS in rural and economically weaker regions to encourage participation;
(c) the steps being taken to ensure PACS to set up and run fuel stations that have access to the necessary infrastructure, including land and storage facilities; and
(d) how allowing PACS to operate petrol/diesel outlets and LPG distributorships will benefit farmers and rural communities?

(a) whether a portal named India Disaster Resource Network has been launched to provide updates on availability of disaster management equipment up to the district level across the country, if so, the details thereof;
(b) the number of States and districts enlisted in the India Disaster Resource Network database; and 
(c) the objective of this network along with the manner in which it would prove beneficial during disasters?

(a) the number of private Engineering Colleges and MBA Colleges which are defunct and not operating currently;
(b) the steps taken to facilitate these Colleges to recommence their academic activities; and
(c) whether there is any plan to promote and assist alternative utilisation of these infrastructure to foster national growth, if their standard is below par for continuing academic activities?

(a) the steps taken by Government to speed up and strengthen the process of insolvency resolution;
(b) the percentage of recovery in the last three years through National Company Law Tribunal (NCLT) and National Company Law Appellate Tribunal (NCLAT); and
(c) the average time taken by NCLT and NCLAT in resolving the cases?

(a) the number of MSMEs that existed till 2013;
(b) the year wise registration of MSMEs since 2019; 
(c) increase in export of MSMEs products in last three years; and
(d) the incentives provided by Government to MSMEs for promoting exports?
